<%# The genre picker, wherever an event's genres are chosen — the capture card, the
    hand-entry page, the admin event editor. One partial because the configuration below
    is what makes it work and every option of it has to match on all three.

    `options` is empty by default so the capture card can render an EMPTY listbox and
    have the browser clone the page's one copy into it (see captures/show +
    capture_controller.js); every other caller passes the list. %>
<%# locals: (name:, id:, value:, chip_src:, label:, badge: nil, options: []) %>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall">
  <%# The label names the field with `for` and must NOT wrap it, unlike an ordinary
      field. The gem draws a selection as a chip inside the field, and a tap on one
      targets the chip — inside a wrapping label that is a click on the label, so the
      browser forwards activation to the labelled input as a second click at the same
      coordinates, defeating the chip's remover. The gem ids the input with a random
      uuid unless given one, so the label needs an id the caller can build. %>
  <label class="field-label flex gap-small align-baseline" for="<%= id %>">
    <%= label %>
    <%= badge %>
  </label>
  <div class="input-wrapper flex genre-combobox">
    <%# Free text on purpose, and the reason the field submits NAMES where every other
        combobox in the app submits ids: a poster names genres the taxonomy has never
        seen, and the gem sends a newly-typed one under the same field name as the
        picked ones — so ids would arrive mixed in with raw text, with a genre called
        "12" indistinguishable from Genre#12. The options exist so a genre we already
        carry is picked rather than respelt.

        `mobile_at` is the width at or below which the gem swaps its inline listbox for
        a modal <dialog>; a width no viewport can be under keeps the listbox everywhere.
        On a phone the dialog covers the screen from the middle down and still shows
        fewer options than the dropdown it replaces, because the software keyboard eats
        the bottom of it.

        Sync options and not a src, so typing filters what is already here: a request
        per keystroke answers a query the user has usually typed past by the time it
        lands, and on mobile data the late answer overwrites the current list. %>
    <%= combobox_tag name, options, value: value, id: id,
          mobile_at: "0px", free_text: true, multiselect_chip_src: chip_src,
          placeholder: t("genres.combobox.placeholder"),
          dialog_label: t("genres.combobox.placeholder") do |combobox| %>
      <% combobox.customize_fieldset class: 'flex-grow' %>
      <% combobox.customize_input class: 'flex-grow' %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
